  "implemented": [
    "Explicit owner and capability-scope registries with fixed capacity and generation-checked re-registration.",
    "Bounded jobs carry purpose, capability scope, resource budget, progress, and lifecycle.",
    "Queued/running/suspended/completed/failed/cancelled transitions are checked; progress cannot regress or exceed its total.",
    "Scope revoke and owner exit cancel matching nonterminal jobs; stale scope generations cannot be reused.",
    "No state transition creates a broader scope; no arbitrary callback or work executor is present."
  ],
  "limitations": [
    "Registrations are not authenticated by a kernel/runtime authority; identifiers are model inputs, not capabilities.",
    "Resource budgets are stored and validated as nonzero but not enforced against real execution.",
    "No real download, sync, indexing, AI, update, import/export, process, or session consumer is integrated.",
    "Owner exit cancels associated work; policy for surviving an app-window close is not defined by this primitive.",
    "This is a PARTIAL host-tested model, not native runtime enforcement or release evidence."
  ]
}
